Linyaps Rust Debian packaging
=============================

The package is built with dh-rust against crate source packages from the
Debian Cargo registry.  Cargo is configured by dh-rust to remain offline;
network downloads during the package build are not supported.

The feature-level Build-Depends list is the union of the direct external
dependencies declared by the workspace crates and the active bundled crate.
It is kept in debian/control because apt must resolve build dependencies
before debian/rules can run.  dh-rust's X-Cargo-Crates mapping then assigns
the application crates to the two binary packages.

The dependency floors follow Debian sid as of 2026-08-17.  Trixie cannot be
used without a substantially larger port because it has no fuser package and
ships an older gix API.  The supplemental package repository is still needed
for am-fs-core, oci-spec, ostrya, ostrya-core, rustls-rustcrypto and serde-yml,
which are not currently packaged in Debian sid.

This upstream workspace contains private application crates and the bundled
am-fs-erofs crate.  The vendor/gix-transport directory is retained as an
upstream source snapshot but is no longer selected by Cargo; gix now uses the
transport supplied by its Debian package.  The bundled sources' licenses are
recorded in debian/copyright.  External Rust dependencies must be supplied by
the librust-*-dev packages listed in debian/control.

The ll-init executable is intentionally rebuilt with crt-static after both the
normal build and the test phase.  It runs as PID 1 inside an application
container and must not depend on libraries from the host or container image.
